","html_url":"https://github.com/Mewlkor","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mewlkor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mewlkor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mewlkor/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mewlkor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mewlkor/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mewlkor/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mewlkor/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mewlkor/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mewlkor/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-11T10:17:35Z","updated_at":"2025-04-11T10:17:35Z","body":"I did some more testing on this. It seems this is just a symptom of more general transparency handling issues. When rendering transparnet object only the viewport the object is contained in is considered but not other viewports that overlap. Probably since usualy that is not a problem because opaque objects don't need to consider what is behind them. \nSo there needs to be a way to pass in the layered viewport textures so the transparency calculations can be done correctly.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2796485552/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]